II. Functional Summary of Mint-to Logic™ as Shown in the Demo
Stage	Functional Action	Purpose / Governance Mechanic
1. Mint Phase	Creation of a “Mint Unit” (one-time validation key) with unique ID (e.g., 9F46-1G7J).	Establishes a traceable, secured digital object defining intent and origin.
2. Validation Phase	“Choose once. Validate once. Burn forever.™” — each action validated through ValiPass™.	Ensures a single verifiable intent and prevents replay or reuse.
3. Behavioral Application	Mint Unit used to verify a real-world interaction (ticket purchase, vote, access credential).	Behavioral governance and authorship validation within cyberspace.
4. Burn Phase	Upon completion or failure, Mint Unit is destroyed (“burned”).	Prevents duplication, fraud, and unauthorized reuse of digital identity tokens.
5. Audit and Lifecycle Management	Each unit logged and tracked in threat-based lifecycle ( low → critical ).	Enables recursive behavioral records and forensic traceability.
